msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Installation and Environment Configuration\n"
"\n"
"## 1. Overview\n"
"\n"
"This document describes how to install Triton-Ascend and configure the environment. Triton-Ascend is a Triton backend for Ascend NPUs, enabling developers to write high-performance operators using the Triton language and run them on Ascend NPUs.\n"
"\n"
"## 2. Environment Requirements\n"
"\n"
"Before installing Triton-Ascend, ensure the following environment requirements are met:\n"
"\n"
"- **Operating System**: Ubuntu 20.04 or later, or other Linux distributions compatible with CANN.\n"
"- **Python Version**: Python 3.8 or later.\n"
"- **CANN Version**: CANN 6.2 or later.\n"
"- **Ascend NPU**: Atlas A2/A3/950 series or other Ascend NPU hardware supported by CANN.\n"
"- **PyTorch**: PyTorch 2.0 or later (optional, required only when using TorchNPU).\n"
"\n"
"## 3. Installation Steps\n"
"\n"
"### 3.1 Install CANN\n"
"\n"
"1. Download the CANN installation package from the [Ascend community](https://www.hiascend.com/).\n"
"2. Follow the CANN installation guide to install CANN.\n"
"3. After installation, configure the CANN environment variables:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"source /usr/local/Ascend/ascend-toolkit/set_env.sh\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 3.2 Install Triton-Ascend\n"
"\n"
"You can install Triton-Ascend in the following ways:\n"
"\n"
"#### Method 1: Install from Source Code\n"
"\n"
"1. Clone the Triton-Ascend repository:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"git clone https://github.com/Ascend/Triton-Ascend.git\n"
"cd Triton-Ascend\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"2. Install dependencies:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"pip install -r requirements.txt\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"3. Build and install:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"python setup.py install\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"#### Method 2: Install Using pip\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"pip install triton-ascend\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 3.3 Install TorchNPU (Optional)\n"
"\n"
"If you need to use Triton-Ascend with PyTorch, install TorchNPU:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"pip install torch-npu\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## 4. Environment Configuration\n"
"\n"
"### 4.1 Configure Ascend NPU Environment Variables\n"
"\n"
"Add the following environment variables to your shell configuration file (e.g., `~/.bashrc`):\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"export ASCEND_HOME=/usr/local/Ascend\n"
"export ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME=${ASCEND_HOME}/ascend-toolkit\n"
"export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME}/lib64:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}\n"
"export PATH=${ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME}/bin:${PATH}\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 4.2 Verify Installation\n"
"\n"
"Run the following Python code to verify that Triton-Ascend is installed correctly:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton_ascend\n"
"\n"
"# Check that the Ascend backend is registered\n"
"print(triton.backends.backends)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If the output contains `ascend`, the installation is successful.\n"
"\n"
"## 5. Common Issues\n"
"\n"
"### 5.1 CANN Environment Variables Not Configured\n"
"\n"
"**Issue**: When running Triton-Ascend, an error similar to the following occurs:\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"RuntimeError: Failed to initialize Ascend runtime. Please check CANN installation.\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**: Ensure that the CANN environment variables are correctly configured:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"source /usr/local/Ascend/ascend-toolkit/set_env.sh\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 5.2 Version Incompatibility\n"
"\n"
"**Issue**: Triton-Ascend fails to compile or run due to version incompatibility with CANN.\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**: Check the version compatibility matrix between Triton-Ascend and CANN, and install a compatible version.\n"
"\n"
"## 6. Next Steps\n"
"\n"
"After completing the installation, you can refer to the following documents:\n"
"\n"
"- [Quick Start Guide](./quick_start.md)\n"
"- [Operator Development Guide](./operator_development_guide.md)\n"
"- [Debugging Guide](./debug_guide.md)\n"

msgid "安装指南"
msgstr "Installation Guide"

msgid "**Triton-Ascend**是适配华为Ascend处理器的Triton优化版本，主要用于提供高效的核函数自动调优、算子编译及部署能力，支持Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950系列产品，兼容Triton核心语法的同时，针对昇腾NPU特性进行了深度优化，包括自动解析核函数参数、优化内存访问逻辑、完善安全部署机制等。帮助用户在昇腾平台上快速开发和部署高性能计算任务。"
msgstr "**Triton-Ascend** is an optimized version of Triton adapted for Huawei Ascend processors, primarily designed to provide efficient automatic kernel tuning, operator compilation, and deployment capabilities. It supports Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950 series products and, while remaining compatible with core Triton syntax, has been deeply optimized for Ascend NPU features, including automatic parsing of kernel parameters, optimization of memory access logic, and enhancement of secure deployment mechanisms. It helps users rapidly develop and deploy high-performance computing tasks on the Ascend platform."

